id: divine-counter
name: Divine Counter
type: counter
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 2
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/round
# A God Maneuver: open where an effect grants it, only in God Ki, its 2(T) paid in Divine Ki Points (maneuvers.mjs
# whyNotGod, spendManeuverCost). Taken in Respond against an attack at you (chat.mjs playDivineCounter): that attack held,
# and a Basic Attack out of sequence at its maker offered on its card. Through a Health Threshold or Defeated by it, their
# attack is cancelled - the Ki Points, Divine Ki Points and Capacity it took given back, its Actions not. Otherwise, or
# let through, it goes on, answered with your Dodge.
godManeuver: true
divineCounter: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A God Maneuver: against an attack at you, a Basic Attack at its maker out of sequence - through a Health Threshold or
  Defeated, their attack is cancelled, its Ki Points and Capacity back.
text: >
  Divine Counter [1/Round]: Repel an enemy’s attack with holy power.
  –Maneuver Type: Counter
  –Action Cost: 1 Counter Action
  –DKP Cost: 2(T)
  –Effect: If you are targeted by an Opponent’s Attacking Maneuver, use the Basic Attack Maneuver against that Opponent as
  an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. If this Attacking Maneuver knocks your Opponent through a Health Threshold or Defeats them,
  their Attacking Maneuver is canceled. They regain any Ki Points and Capacity Rate spent on that Attacking Maneuver, but
  still lose the Action Cost.
